pythonic APIs). Also, CuPy considers the Cython layer as an implementation detail and has never guaranteed API stability, so things could break between releases. It would be better to avoid accessing CuPy's Cython modules.

To help nvmath-python assess the demand of stabilizing the bindings by its 1.0 release, it'd be great if you could file an issue in the nvmath-python repo, with your intended usage. 

